# Application preview pipeline

Put rules that must apply to **every** Storage/repo HTML here — not in one-off template edits.

| Concern | Place |
|---------|--------|
| Letter-field accordion sections (DATE / SUBJECT / …) | `application_document_placeholders.section_label` (+ `ui_group` fallback via `sectionTitleFromUiGroup` / `buildCatalogLetterFieldRows`). No per-app React. |
| Ward / plot / village-TPS grammar | `applicationCatalog.ts` formatters + `normalizePlotTypeLabelsInTemplateHtml` |
| Suburb from ward/region | `resolveCatalogPlaceholderValue` for `suburb` / `{{SUBURB}}` using `save_plot_details.region` or `inferLocationFromWard` from `app/lib/projectDocumentAutofill/utils.ts` |
| BP address lines 1–3 | `mapToPdfFieldValues` in `applicationPreview.ts` — alias `{{BP_ADDRESS_LINE_*}}` from `resolveBuildingProposalOffice` (same as `$project_addressline*_BuildingProposal`) |
| Empty address / unreplaced token lines | `removeEmptyAddressParagraphs` (and siblings) in `application-preview-html/route.ts` |
| Date/CC orphans, letterhead first page, margins | `injectPaginatedStyles` in `applicationPreview.ts` |
| Per-doc letterhead/QR on/off | `application_documents` catalog flags (`show_letterhead`, `letterhead_source`) |
| Letterhead image URL | Strictly `application_documents.letterhead_source`: `owner` → owner URL; `architect_or_ls` / `consultant` → that appointed profile URL. **Never** viewer JWT, never cross-party fallback, never HTML/CSS scrape. Missing URL → no image and no reserved logo/footer space. Multi-doc apps (Document Checklist) resolve the selected document’s source via `templateTypeForLetterheadSource` |
| DSC stamp slot in HTML | Only when `application_documents.sign` requires it; class `.dsc-stamp-slot` (owner: `--owner`) |

## Letterhead: assigned person only (every application)

1. Resolve letterhead from `letterhead_source` / acceptance vs appointment — **that party only**.
2. Acceptance / `consultant` source: use `consultantLetterheadUrl`. If empty → **blank** (do **not** use owner).
3. Appointment / `owner` source: use `ownerLetterheadUrl`. If empty → **blank**.
4. When blank: omit letterhead CSS background **and** collapse first-page top / footer clearance (no empty band for a missing logo).
5. Do not invent a default/shared letterhead image for any catalog document.

## Suburb from ward (BMC To-block)

`{{SUBURB}}` must never stay blank when ward/region is known.

1. Read `project.save_plot_details.region` (`City` | `Western` | `Eastern`).
2. If empty, `inferLocationFromWard(save_plot_details.ward)` (ward keys like `L Ward`).
3. Print the region string as-is (`City` / `Western` / `Eastern`) — **do not** append “Suburb”.

Reuse the existing ward→zone→region tables in `projectDocumentAutofill/utils.ts`; do not duplicate a second ward map in HTML.

## Building Proposal address lines (Address Line 1/2/3)

Same logic as Building Permission / appointment letters:

1. Always fetch `building_proposal_offices` in `buildApplicationPreviewContext` (do **not** gate on `appointment_letter` / `includeConsultantProfiles`).
2. Resolve office via `resolveBuildingProposalOffice(region, ward, offices)`.
3. Fill `{{BP_ADDRESS_LINE_1}}` / `_2` / `_3` (and legacy `$project_addressline*_BuildingProposal`) from that office’s `line1`/`line2`/`line3` in `mapToPdfFieldValues`.
4. Empty lines are dropped by `removeEmptyAddressParagraphs` after substitution.

Do not invent a second address source for Document Checklist or other catalog forms.

## Forms vs letters

- Letters (`letter_variant` appointment/acceptance) get shared CSS from `html/_shared/application-templates.css`.
- Forms skip that inject so large tables can split. Form keep-together must target **closing blocks only** (`.closing`, `.sig`, `.cc`) — never `break-inside: avoid` on every `p`/`table`.
- Wrap `Thanking you` / `Yours Faithfully` + `.sig` (+ optional `.cc`) in `.closing` for structure/DSC markup. On **letterheaded forms**, do **not** use `break-inside`/`break-before: avoid` on `.closing` / `.sig` / signer blocks — nested avoids make Paged.js drop most of the body (empty page, signer remnant only). Densify rhythm for page-1 fit; allow normal splitting if content still overflows.
- Letterheaded **forms** (Document Checklist annexures, etc.): first content line (`ANNEXURE …`, title, or `To,`) must clear the logo with the **same** first-page inset as appointment/acceptance — **115pt** `@page :first` top + **0** content top pad (`useLetterheadFirstPageClearance`). Do **not** add per-HTML `padding-top` / spacer paragraphs above ANNEXURE.
- Letterhead **footer** clearance: bottom `@page` margin must keep body/signature/C.C. above the scanned footer (gold bar / address / contact). Letterheaded forms use ~**84pt** bottom (tuned with dense annexure CSS for page-1 fit + DSC 180×60 + long multi-CTS). Prefer densifying body/meta/to-block/closing rhythm (meta values ~9pt, wrap `overflow-wrap:anywhere`) before cutting footer clearance further; overlapping the letterhead footer is wrong — spill to page 2 if content still cannot fit.
- Long multi-CTS meta values: pipeline densify CSS must wrap tightly (`.meta-table td:last-child` / `.value-bold`) so closing + DSC stay visible. Do **not** reintroduce `break-inside:avoid` on `.closing`/`.sig` to “keep” them — that drops the body.

## Letter-field sections (every catalog application)

1. Accordion titles come from `application_document_placeholders.section_label` (document-scoped; Concession custom titles stay valid).
2. If `section_label` is null, `buildCatalogLetterFieldRows` uses `sectionTitleFromUiGroup(ui_group)`: subject→Subject, reference→Reference, consultant→Consultant, client→Client, office→Addressee, other→Other fields.
3. `groupCatalogLetterFieldRows` only falls back to a single **Details** accordion when **no** row has a resolved section label.
4. New apps: seed `section_label` (and/or correct `ui_group`) in SQL — never add Application Details branches per `application_type`.

## `{{APPOINTMENT_DATE}}` = application created date

1. Catalog `appointment_date` resolves from `application_created_at` (ISO) via `formatCatalogDateDmy`.
2. Application Details / preview pass `applicationCreatedAt` into `catalogPlaceholderFieldMap`.
3. Preview hard-fills `{{APPOINTMENT_DATE}}` if still empty (created_at or today).
4. Used on Document Checklist Structural / Site Supervisor memos (and any future consultant HTML with the token).

## `{{BUILDING_NO}}` = proposal number

1. Catalog placeholder `building_no` → `projects` / `project_info->>proposalNo` (same as `file_no` / `proposal_number`).
2. Computed fallback in `resolveCatalogPlaceholderValue` + preview hard-fill from `project_info.proposalNo` if the DB row is still stale `computed`.
3. Used on Document Checklist: Notice for Start of Work, Intimation upto Plinth, Development Completion Certificate.

## DigiSatbara / `{{DATE_OF_PRC}}` (every checklist/PAC consumer)

1. Extract `downloadDate` from primary PR card footer (`मिळकत पत्रिका डाउनलोड दिनांक`) via `parsePrCardDownloadDate` / `enrichPrCardDownloadDate` — not the DSC timestamp.
2. `mergeSavePlot` writes `save_plot_details.prcDownloadDate` (prefer primary; else any remaining PR with a date).
3. Project Library Save and Property Details Save **PUT** that key on the project (incl. draft projects).
4. Preview/Letter fields: `mergeSavePlotDetailsForCatalog` overlays local draft over DB so checklist sees the date without a second save. `fetchApplicationPreviewHtmlRaw` also hard-fills `{{DATE_OF_PRC}}` from `prcDownloadDate` if the catalog row is missing.
5. Put resolution in `applicationCatalog` / preview pipeline — **not** per-application HTML hacks.

## Static vs filled chrome (every application)

- Labels like `C.C. to:`, `To,`, `Subject:`, `Reference:` are **static** — normal weight / `.cc-label` / plain text. Never `.value-bold`.
- `.value-bold` is only for substituted project/applicant values (names, addresses, CTS, dates, file nos.).
- Computed role prose on C.C. (`{{OWNER_OR_DEVELOPER}}`) may use `.bold`, not `.value-bold`.
- Architect C.C. / signer tokens: always resolve via Architect then L.S. roster row — never the Structural Engineer / Plumber / Site Supervisor signer. Use `{{ARCHITECT_OR_LS_ROLE}}` (single role), `{{ARCHITECT_OR_LS_REG_LABEL}}`, `{{ARCHITECT_LS_REG_NO}}`, `{{ARCHITECT_LS_VALIDITY}}` — never hardcode “Architect/ Licensed Surveyor”.

## Plot slash-lists

Rewrite at normalize time from `plotBelongsTo` so old HTML with four slash fields still collapses. Prefer teaching new HTML to use `{{PLOT_CS_CTS_NO}}` / `{{VILLAGE_DIVISION}}` for **inline prose**; meta-table rows keep slash lists so key/value split. Letter fields UI uses `collapsePlotBelongsPlaceholdersForLetterFields` so the panel shows one survey + one place row.
